# KNN Pipeline and GridSearchCV Mini Project

This mini-project was completed as part of my Machine Learning internship preparation.

## Objective

Build a K-Nearest Neighbors classification pipeline and compare different K values and weighting methods using cross-validation.

## Dataset

Scikit-learn Wine Classification Dataset

## Workflow

- Loaded and explored the Wine dataset
- Split the data into training and test sets
- Built a Pipeline using StandardScaler and KNeighborsClassifier
- Tested K values: 3, 5, 7, 11, and 21
- Compared uniform and distance weighting
- Used 5-fold cross-validation with GridSearchCV
- Selected the best hyperparameter combination
- Evaluated the best model on the test set
- Visualized K vs Mean CV Accuracy

## Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas
- Matplotlib
- Scikit-learn

## Key Learning

KNN is sensitive to feature scale because it uses distance to find nearest neighbors.

Increasing K does not always improve performance continuously. In this experiment, moderate-to-higher K values performed better, while uniform and distance weighting gave similar results overall.

